  "narrative": "H96 response deadline: the KY CRISPR-library PTEN-loss/STAT3 claim remains unresolved. Discovery R93 gave signed estimate +0.158 with 95% interval +0.063 to +0.253; independent validation R166 gave signed estimate +0.230 with independent interval +0.077 to +0.382. Both estimates are direction-consistent with stronger STAT3 dependency among PTEN-loss cells and exclude zero, but the validated lower bound is below the +0.10 clinically meaningful benchmark. Therefore I keep H96 unresolved and close the subgroup investigation because the central PTEN-loss/STAT3 association is already accepted and validated, while the KY-specific clinically meaningful threshold is not met. This does not establish absence of a KY-library effect; it only limits the strength of the within-dataset claim. The overall conclusions remain supported within-dataset associations, not causal or externally generalized findings.",
  "research_notes": "Final scientific report. Supported accepted within-dataset associations: (1) MSI-high cells show much stronger dependency_WRN, H6 with discovery R6 and validation R52, reinforced by many context-independent and co-mutation-stratum estimates; (2) SMARCA4-loss cells show much stronger dependency_SMARCA2, H8 with validation R13, reinforced across batches, libraries, QC, lineage, TP53, CDKN2A, STK11, KEAP1, ARID1A contexts; (3) KEAP1-loss cells show much weaker dependency_NFE2L2, accepted via H20 with evidence R9 and R39, reinforced across tp53_loss, msi_high, library, lineage, STK11, CDKN2A, QC, batch, ARID1A and SMARCA4 contexts; (4) TP53-loss cells show much weaker dependency_USP7, H15 with validation R26, reinforced across avana/KY libraries, CDKN2A, STK11, MTAP, MSI, QC, lineage, batch, ARID1A, KEAP1 and SMARCA4 contexts; (5) PTEN-loss cells show stronger dependency_STAT3, H93 with validation R90, reinforced across many contexts and accepted/validated in TP53-loss cells via H102 with R99 and R179. Negative findings support relative specificity rather than universal dependency: KRAS mutation was not clinically benchmark-supported for dependency_KRAS, dependency_RIT1, dependency_EGFR, or dependency_STAT3; BRAF V600E was not supported for dependency_BRAF; EGFR and ERBB2 amplification were not supported for their respective dependencies; TP53 loss was not associated with dependency_MDM2; ARID1A loss was not associated with dependency_SMARCA2; MYC amplification repeatedly failed clinically benchmarking; MTAP loss was not clinically meaningful for USP7 or MDM2 dependency; BRCA2 loss was not associated with WRN, DHX9, or POLR2A dependency; constructed research markers were generally null. Interaction claims were largely not clinically benchmarked, and H148 TP53-loss by high mutation burden interaction on USP7 was rejected after validation contradiction. Unresolved uncertainty: H96 KY-library PTEN-loss/STAT3 remains unresolved because discovery and validation lower bounds fall below +0.10; several narrow PTEN-loss/STAT3 contexts remain deferred, including H162-H165; direct interaction or co-mutation context claims generally remain non-decision-relevant unless a later estimate crosses threshold. Biological interpretation, causality, and generalizability remain uncertain. The most informative next analysis, if investigation capacity is allocated, would be targeted validation or additional estimation of H156, PTEN-loss dependency_STAT3 in TP53-loss CDKN2A-wild-type cells, because it is biologically plausible and its discovery lower bound is closest to the clinically meaningful benchmark among co-mutation residual contexts; H163 is an alternative closest to threshold but is more a QC-context check. No new claim is accepted beyond the central within-dataset associations described above."
}
